WEBVTT

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.990
Mimi, bring some water.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:44.960
Yes.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:06.690
Geez.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.350
Vodka means water in Russian.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.720
And you prefer it this way, right?

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.210
W-Wait a minute... Where is Maeno-kun?

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.190
I gave him some work.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.330
Work?

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.700
Business.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.290
Hello.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.790
This is Asougi Consulting.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.020
E-Excuse me.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.420
Is something wrong?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.960
I can't find it.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.220
Find what?

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.980
I'm very good at finding things.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:19.840
I might be able to help.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:23.930
I'm looking for an angel.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.600
A stamp?

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.380
Sorry for not mentioning it earlier.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.400
I am Kodaka Saburou from the main office of Shinuma Funds.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.210
Thank you.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.140
Why is a large corporation like yours coming to us?

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:46.920
This isn't our specialty.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.580
Wouldn't it be better to ask an expert about something like this?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.080
It's a special stamp.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.550
We have heard rumors that the owner of this stamp lives in Shinjuku.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:00.090
And that...

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.090
this place has access to underground information.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.110
You just have to find the owner.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.850
We will conduct the negotiations.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.500
Really, something like this—

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.610
Of course, we'll do it.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.430
This place has the widest view of Tokyo's skies.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.020
Here I feel like I could even find an angel.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:27.820
P-Perhaps.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.010
Really...

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.830
Will you help me?

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.870
Of course.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.590
Why did you try to turn him down?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.640
Secretary General Androvsky has decided to come, it says.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.820
He's coming here because the Berlin Wall fell. That's pretty tough.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.460
Don't change the subject.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.850
Even if we can't find it, we'll still get our per diem.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:50.810
Isn't that a great job?

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.850
Somehow...

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.560
And of course, we do have some leads, right?

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.570
Sensei...

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.600
Hi, Rin-chan.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.810
Hi. Where is sensei?

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.010
At the usual place.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:11.330
Thank you.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:13.540
Sensei.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.560
Hi, Asougi-san.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.090
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.170
Do you know anything about the Sutherland stamp?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.180
I am the worst human being.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.180
There are lots of people who are worse.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.830
I should have stayed in academics,

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.940
but I went into the futures market.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.700
Then the bubble broke, and I lost everything.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.200
Even though I've ended up here,

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.040
I still can't discard my pride.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.700
I am the worst human being.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:52.410
There is something else I can't discard, up here.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.730
If there is something good about this life,

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:02.670
it's realizing that the knowledge I carry is totally useless.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:09.630
Even so, there are people like you who come to me in need of my knowledge.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.930
Honestly, I am very happy.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.770
Sensei.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.970
Do you know about this?

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.030
I guess it was the right idea to talk to you.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.710
The first stamp in Japan.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:30.950
Published in 1871, the Ryuumon stamp.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.500
Look at this.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.900
The beauty of it.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.220
This intricate pattern was made by hand.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:40.030
The product of a craftsman's will and skill.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.510
This is also one of those things I can't discard.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.690
Even though I could probably get enough to live by selling it.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.800
Really, I am the worst human being.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:56.300
It's not that there weren't any stamps before this one.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:56.970
Eh?

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.870
That's the Sutherland stamp.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:05.330
I heard this stamp was published in 1870 by the Sutherland Company,

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.940
but I don't know the details.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.390
There are only a few of them?

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.810
That's right.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:16.530
In the entire country, only about ten of them have been confirmed to exist.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.970
That's a problem.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.490
Only a few confirmed Sutherland stamps,

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:24.890
and we're looking for one that's already been used.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.050
But a used one is less valuable, right?

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.200
Sensei?

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.310
Ah, sorry.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.580
Sutherland stamps are different.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:41.500
Every stamp that has been found up until now has been unused.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:46.360
I do not believe that they were ever used as stamps.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:47.530
It's hopeless?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:53.420
Moreover, most that were found have a face value of one quarter.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:57.340
There's only a single instance with a face value of one.

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.200
Totally hopeless, is it?

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.210
Whose request was this?

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.930
That's a bit...

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.050
You've been helpful.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:08.960
No, I wasn't of much help.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.180
Excuse me.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.240
Yes.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.170
Ah.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:34.360
Is that right?

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.460
I've had an uneasy feeling in my chest recently.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.100
I wonder why?

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.150
Of course I remember.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.920
That's right. That's how it was.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.960
That time too,

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.680
it was an awful night when even an angel would cry.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:06.630
It's great!

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:08.310
I'm going to die!

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:09.720
I'm going to die!

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:18.740
You!

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:34.420
What's wrong?

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:35.560
This.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.760
A Foreign Ministry employee was killed in a hotel.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.510
Look at the picture.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.020
Him?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.060
I am Kodaka Saburou from the head office of Shinuma Funds.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.620
His real name is Yahagi Jun.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:55.050
Kodaka was a fake name.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.280
A Foreign Ministry employee...

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.950
Something strange is going on.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.710
Should we stop with just the advance payment?

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:03.490
Where are you going?

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:06.180
We have to work for the advance.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:08.500
What's with that outfit?

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.750
I think it's going to be fashionable from now on.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:25.220
Hey, have you been watching too many spy movies?

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.690
Don't look this way!

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.730
It's not funny.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:35.530
I have to be really careful about this case.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:36.620
Are the police involved?

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.310
You shouldn't look this way, right?

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.200
Exactly as you said.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.520
I don't know why, but we can't even visit the crime scene.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.580
Anyway, it's pretty bad.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.950
I won't say anymore.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.380
Give it up this time.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.180
It can't be helped.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.530
It's a job.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:57.670
Job?

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:58.530
What—

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:01.740
No, it doesn't matter. I didn't hear anything.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.390
I'll tell people what you did the year before.

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:08.470
Even that's better than this.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.440
It must be really bad for Tamo-chan to be that scared.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:13.410
Rin-chan.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.720
I caught you at the right place.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.650
It's terrible.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.060
Sensei...

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:38.570
The stamps have something to do with this after all?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.230
Someone followed me that time.

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:01.840
Thank you.

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:04.740
This looks like a nice place.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:08.370
Do you use computers?

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:09.730
That's my brother's.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:10.870
You have a brother.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:15.620
He hasn't been back for a week.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.040
You don't have to worry anymore.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.360
It's okay.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.230
It will be over soon.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:44.200
A week ago, my brother said he would end it today, and left.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.700
How many times will you die today?

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.300
How... does she know where I am...

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.630
Who is it?

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:07.590
That was probably...

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:09.510
an angel.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.640
She noticed me.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:33.540
That angel must know where my brother is.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.500
That's why I have to find the angel.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.290
Apos sent you?

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:03.160
What is it?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.080
Um...

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.190
Are you okay?

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:51.280
Maeno-kun.

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:52.530
Rin-san!

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.080
No...

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:53.660
Are you okay?

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.910
D-Don't come near me.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.030
Please.

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:04.750
Don't look.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:15.930
Don't look.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.850
Please.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.940
Aren't you drinking too much?

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:33.740
Must have been your first time.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.450
Seeing that.

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:38.660
The first time must be rough.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:40.830
Why?

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.860
Why did something like that happen?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.990
We can't die.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:50.670
You too?

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:53.680
Because of the Fruit of Immortality.

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:56.980
Why it has that effect,

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:59.410
or whether it comes from this world, we don't know.

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:04.100
But when it entered our bodies, we became immortal.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:08.780
In a forgotten time long ago, both Rin and I

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.940
were exposed to it before we noticed.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:16.970
Usually, if I just told you all of a sudden, you wouldn't believe me,

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:19.530
but you saw it.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.880
You should decide.

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.700
If you want to quit, Rin won't say anything.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:29.960
I'm sure.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:33.150
Me either.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.860
I'm going home for today.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:48.130
Mimi.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:53.990
See you tomorrow.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.210
Idiot!

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.990
Don't go back! Drink!

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:02.330
I already...

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.180
Shut up!

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:05.260
Are you saying you won't drink my booze?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:06.710
Seriously?

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:19.850
Apos.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:25.020
Quite an unpredictable queen.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.600
Speaking of which, an angel was born.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.780
It's silly asking a question like that, no?

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:41.280
Of course I made it.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.210
You hate angels, don't you?

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:51.350
Because you are...

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.300
one of the immortals.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.110
This is...

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.470
It can't be...

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.180
An angel.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.670
Where is Rin-san?

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:02.870
Don't worry.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.320
The police have her in custody now.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.480
The police?

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.710
But I heard the man who was killed was just a pimp.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.320
I don't know.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:13.040
Anyway, she's an important witness in a serial murder case.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.690
That's...

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:16.070
What should I do?

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:16.960
Hey.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.760
You've been working at Rin's place for a long time, right?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:20.800
It's only been a year.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:24.230
Even babies can leave the womb faster than that.

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.300
It's enough time for you to grow up.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:28.590
Do your best.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.410
You know these people, right?

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:48.910
Like I said, I don't know anything.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.860
A Foreign Ministry employee.

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:53.580
Female prostitutes.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.850
Someone with a special relationship to them.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:58.550
And a Chinese illegal immigrant.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:03.930
These seemingly unrelated people have something surprising in common.

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:05.620
What's that?

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:09.680
I was thinking you'd tell me that.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:39.940
Ow-Ow-Ow...

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.300
Endure it.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.850
It's an honorable wound.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:46.210
That Yanagisawa-san was mean.

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:48.730
Telling me to do my best just because he couldn't act.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:50.150
Yanagisawa?

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:51.860
Ah, Tamo-chan.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.520
So, did you learn something?

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:55.860
The Chinese man who was killed, Lee,

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.050
he belonged to a Chinese Snakehead mafia.

00:20:58.570 --> 00:20:59.950
When I was looking into that...

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:01.040
You became like this.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:01.570
Ouch!

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.370
Not only illegal immigrants,

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:07.650
they are also involved with other smuggling activities.

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:09.860
Anything in common with the other victims?

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.290
Well, the pimp might be related, but...

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:16.290
I don't think the Foreign Ministry employee is related.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.280
What about the Sutherland stamp?

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:19.870
I couldn't figure that part out either.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:23.450
It's like a jigsaw puzzle.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:25.980
Eventually we'll find a new piece,

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.650
and maybe the picture will become obvious.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:29.310
Another murder?

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:31.050
Probably.

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:34.460
You can go home.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.270
You're releasing me?

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.770
We're not holding you in custody anymore.

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:40.310
Someone else got killed.

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:46.170
Don't do that again!

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:47.810
Doing that on purpose.

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:49.990
An American named James McAndrew.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:51.080
Thank you.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.030
Shut up!

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.390
A grasshopper.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:07.860
A kiddy drink that tastes like toothpaste.

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:09.760
You can say whatever you want...

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:13.170
since I haven't had a request from you in a long time.

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:14.280
And?

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:16.280
It's going to be expensive.

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:19.620
Give me that.

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:48.220
Hey.

00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:50.940
Where is the info?

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:52.730
You're so mean.

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:53.720
Who's the mean one?

00:22:57.110 --> 00:22:58.600
If you want this...

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:05.480
You'll have to get it yourself.

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:20.910
I'm back.

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:21.750
Welcome back.

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:22.800
Rin-san.

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.750
I was so worried!

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.170
We got a call from Yanagisawa-san that you'd been released,

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:28.890
but you didn't come back.

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:30.810
Sorry.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:31.800
Thank you.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:36.680
It looks like we can see the picture at last.

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:38.990
You met that woman, right?

00:23:38.990 --> 00:23:40.400
I hate her.

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:42.060
Her information is expensive.

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:44.190
This time it was worth it.

00:23:45.830 --> 00:23:49.420
The victim last night, James McAndrew, was quite an infamous guy.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:51.900
Alexander Koschiuszko?

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:53.980
A radical Stalinist.

00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:57.120
A member of the Red March.

00:23:57.620 --> 00:23:58.600
Don't tell me...

00:23:58.600 --> 00:23:59.080
Probably.

00:23:59.630 --> 00:24:00.740
Um...

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.580
I don't see it at all.

00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:07.450
You know that Secretary General Androvsky is pro-Western, right?

00:24:07.450 --> 00:24:08.680
Yes.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:10.500
He's popular in the west,

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:13.340
but lots of people inside the Soviet Union are unhappy with him.

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:15.100
The Red March.

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:18.650
It's an extremely violent faction.

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:23.070
They are trying to eliminate the reformist Secretary General,

00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:25.390
and to maintain Communism.

00:24:26.470 --> 00:24:28.070
Even if they need to do it by force.

00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:29.980
Then... in other words...

00:24:30.590 --> 00:24:31.860
Assassination.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:34.700
What are you doing?

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:36.930
What? Calling the police.

00:24:36.930 --> 00:24:38.320
We don't have any proof.

00:24:38.770 --> 00:24:39.840
But...

00:24:39.840 --> 00:24:41.200
The police know too.

00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:44.920
There is nothing we can do.

00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:52.560
A call from your girlfriend?

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:54.260
It's not like that.

00:24:54.260 --> 00:24:55.010
My client.

00:24:55.550 --> 00:24:57.310
Then go, quickly.

00:24:57.310 --> 00:24:58.190
Yes.

00:24:58.190 --> 00:24:59.620
See you.

00:25:03.560 --> 00:25:05.060
You drove Kouki away, didn't you?

00:25:05.510 --> 00:25:06.580
You knew?

00:25:06.580 --> 00:25:07.900
What happened?

00:25:07.900 --> 00:25:09.460
Our natural enemy.

00:25:09.460 --> 00:25:10.400
An angel?

00:25:10.400 --> 00:25:11.380
That's right.

00:25:11.380 --> 00:25:12.300
I saw him.

00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:13.510
That's...

00:25:13.510 --> 00:25:14.740
You weren't mistaken?

00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:16.570
But you're okay...

00:25:18.160 --> 00:25:19.570
No doubt about it.

00:25:20.200 --> 00:25:22.080
My body reacted to him.

00:25:22.080 --> 00:25:22.980
You know, right?

00:25:23.540 --> 00:25:26.570
Also, the police haven't said anything about it officially,

00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:30.750
but the word "Angel" was written in blood at every crime scene.

00:25:31.460 --> 00:25:32.590
I saw it too.

00:25:33.040 --> 00:25:34.500
I'm scared, Rin.

00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:36.580
I...

00:25:36.580 --> 00:25:37.420
It's okay.

00:25:38.270 --> 00:25:39.140
I'll defeat him.

00:25:40.420 --> 00:25:41.720
For our sake.

00:25:44.040 --> 00:25:46.300
I wonder where the angel went?

00:25:46.300 --> 00:25:47.650
I wonder.

00:25:47.650 --> 00:25:49.310
I did look for him.

00:25:50.020 --> 00:25:50.930
Really?

00:25:54.410 --> 00:25:56.870
Don't you believe that angels exist?

00:25:57.420 --> 00:25:59.450
I-It's not like that.

00:26:00.310 --> 00:26:01.700
Look into my eyes.

00:26:02.650 --> 00:26:03.790
Do you believe in angels?

00:26:03.990 --> 00:26:05.360
Believe...

00:26:11.810 --> 00:26:13.540
The angel is your brother.

00:26:15.010 --> 00:26:18.030
That image of your brother disappearing...

00:26:18.030 --> 00:26:19.300
You came to believe that was an angel.

00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:21.380
That's what I think.

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:24.560
I thought...

00:26:24.890 --> 00:26:26.310
you'd believe in me.

00:26:26.980 --> 00:26:27.860
That's what I thought.

00:26:28.330 --> 00:26:29.020
Yuki-chan.

00:26:29.890 --> 00:26:30.620
Yuki-chan!

00:26:38.170 --> 00:26:40.280
Someone must've wanted the stamps.

00:26:41.610 --> 00:26:42.820
Sensei.

00:26:45.920 --> 00:26:47.210
I'm back.

00:26:47.210 --> 00:26:48.330
Welcome back.

00:26:52.110 --> 00:26:53.690
Direct mail?

00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:58.060
Lucky, we can use this again if I peel it off.

00:26:58.060 --> 00:26:59.330
Since it doesn't have a stamp.

00:26:59.870 --> 00:27:00.500
Mimi!

00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:01.430
Am I being too stingy?

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:02.430
No.

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:04.140
It doesn't have a stamp.

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:05.660
It's the Stamp!

00:27:05.660 --> 00:27:07.770
Why didn't I think of that until now?

00:27:07.770 --> 00:27:09.250
It's the Stamp!

00:27:09.250 --> 00:27:10.310
No doubt about it.

00:27:10.310 --> 00:27:12.200
Is something wrong with the postmark?

00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:13.320
Don't you understand?

00:27:13.320 --> 00:27:14.360
Stamp the assassin.

00:27:16.140 --> 00:27:17.400
Ah!

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:21.860
The legendary assassin who asks for stamps as his payment!

00:27:21.860 --> 00:27:22.870
That's it!

00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:25.990
I thought he was only a legend. I didn't even think about it.

00:27:25.990 --> 00:27:27.380
But in that light,

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:30.570
the assassination of the Secretary General and the Sutherland stamp are linked, right?

00:27:30.570 --> 00:27:32.020
What about the woman and the pimp?

00:27:32.020 --> 00:27:35.800
Right, just to get to that Ministry guy, Yahagi?

00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:37.880
It was to make him provide information and cooperation.

00:27:38.320 --> 00:27:39.830
What about the Snakehead?

00:27:39.830 --> 00:27:42.020
Must be a request to smuggle something.

00:27:42.020 --> 00:27:43.040
Smuggle what?

00:27:43.040 --> 00:27:45.640
I don't know, but probably something big.

00:27:46.140 --> 00:27:49.270
Then, who is killing the conspirators?

00:27:50.060 --> 00:27:52.280
In other words, who is the angel?

00:28:09.830 --> 00:28:11.160
You are...

00:28:11.610 --> 00:28:13.380
I don't know anything.

00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:14.560
Someone asked me.

00:28:14.560 --> 00:28:16.920
Here, I'll give this back to you.

00:28:17.250 --> 00:28:18.850
Please, let me go.

00:28:18.850 --> 00:28:22.000
I didn't tell anyone about you, and I won't say anything either.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:22.630
Okay?

00:28:23.670 --> 00:28:26.140
That's right. Let's do something fun.

00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:28.200
You want to do what we were doing that time, right?

00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:30.940
Okay? Here, leave it to me.

00:28:32.320 --> 00:28:33.430
Now...

00:28:51.290 --> 00:28:52.080
Brother!

00:28:55.010 --> 00:28:56.200
Brother, wait!

00:28:57.710 --> 00:28:59.500
No! Brother!

00:29:04.260 --> 00:29:05.100
Brother...

00:29:08.190 --> 00:29:09.170
Sorry.

00:29:10.790 --> 00:29:12.600
For calling you this late.

00:29:13.370 --> 00:29:15.520
But you're the only one I can rely on.

00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:17.650
It's okay.

00:29:18.970 --> 00:29:20.590
It's like you said.

00:29:20.590 --> 00:29:21.690
The angel is my brother.

00:29:21.980 --> 00:29:23.090
No, that's...

00:29:23.090 --> 00:29:24.190
No, listen.

00:29:24.840 --> 00:29:26.500
My brother is the angel.

00:29:26.500 --> 00:29:28.410
He became an angel, and came back.

00:29:33.940 --> 00:29:34.910
That's why...

00:29:35.850 --> 00:29:38.050
you don't have to look for angels anymore.

00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:41.070
I've found my brother.

00:29:41.970 --> 00:29:43.920
That's right.

00:29:44.610 --> 00:29:45.490
So...

00:29:46.560 --> 00:29:47.430
goodbye.

00:29:57.310 --> 00:29:58.350
This is...

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:01.170
Let me borrow your phone.

00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:04.980
Now then.

00:30:08.460 --> 00:30:09.420
This is your brother's, right?

00:30:09.870 --> 00:30:10.570
Yes.

00:30:10.950 --> 00:30:14.520
You might not know it, but it's not a good place.

00:30:15.090 --> 00:30:16.450
I know.

00:30:16.450 --> 00:30:19.810
After my brother started going to that place, he changed.

00:30:19.810 --> 00:30:21.000
Is that right?

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:21.630
Bingo!

00:30:22.180 --> 00:30:24.760
It looks like the disk has been formatted and erased,

00:30:24.760 --> 00:30:26.630
but the data's still there.

00:30:26.630 --> 00:30:27.580
He forgot to delete it?

00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:28.910
You know,

00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:34.150
this is a 16-bit, 40MHz CPU, with 128MB of memory.

00:30:34.150 --> 00:30:37.680
Only the hard drive has been expanded to 300MB.

00:30:37.680 --> 00:30:41.640
Do you think a user like that would forget to delete things?

00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:43.830
Of course it was done on purpose.

00:30:43.830 --> 00:30:46.360
I don't really know about computers, so...

00:30:46.800 --> 00:30:48.210
Probably.

00:30:48.210 --> 00:30:51.010
Now then, what do you think the password is?

00:30:51.390 --> 00:30:52.840
There's only one, right?

00:30:52.840 --> 00:30:53.870
Right.

00:30:54.160 --> 00:30:55.370
"Angel."

00:30:56.890 --> 00:30:58.460
Bingo again.

00:31:00.460 --> 00:31:01.420
This is...

00:31:01.820 --> 00:31:03.870
Looks like information from the police and the Foreign Ministry.

00:31:04.340 --> 00:31:05.920
Yahagi got his hands on this.

00:31:06.740 --> 00:31:09.380
Your brother must be a skilled hacker.

00:31:10.270 --> 00:31:11.330
I don't know.

00:31:12.150 --> 00:31:13.890
My brother didn't say anything.

00:31:15.630 --> 00:31:17.300
We'll leave this to you.

00:31:17.300 --> 00:31:18.770
Maeno-kun, come with me.

00:31:18.900 --> 00:31:19.410
Yes.

00:31:21.340 --> 00:31:24.220
She asked you to look for an angel, right?

00:31:24.220 --> 00:31:25.530
Sorry.

00:31:25.530 --> 00:31:26.770
I meant to tell you.

00:31:27.440 --> 00:31:28.270
It's okay.

00:31:33.800 --> 00:31:37.420
Recently, Mimi told you about the Fruit of Immortality, right?

00:31:37.420 --> 00:31:38.040
Yes.

00:31:39.060 --> 00:31:42.040
When the Fruit of Immortality enters your body, you become immortal.

00:31:42.880 --> 00:31:45.790
But that only applies to women.

00:31:47.380 --> 00:31:48.280
Men...

00:31:49.740 --> 00:31:50.670
become angels.

00:31:51.240 --> 00:31:51.720
Angels?

00:31:52.690 --> 00:31:55.580
They're only called that because their appearance is similar.

00:31:55.580 --> 00:31:57.180
They're not real angels.

00:31:57.650 --> 00:31:59.670
Then, Yuki-chan's brother is...

00:31:59.670 --> 00:32:00.200
Yes.

00:32:02.210 --> 00:32:04.190
He really has become an angel.

00:32:06.050 --> 00:32:10.490
Men who become angels acquire superhuman powers.

00:32:10.490 --> 00:32:14.200
In exchange for that, they only live a short time.

00:32:14.610 --> 00:32:16.950
A short time... how short?

00:32:17.510 --> 00:32:18.900
I don't really know.

00:32:19.770 --> 00:32:22.200
But probably about two or three weeks.

00:32:23.650 --> 00:32:24.930
That's...

00:32:26.740 --> 00:32:29.590
When they become angels, they lose their own will,

00:32:29.590 --> 00:32:31.710
and act according to certain instincts.

00:32:32.640 --> 00:32:36.620
Yuki-chan's brother suppressed his instincts with a strong will,

00:32:36.620 --> 00:32:39.120
and killed all those who tried to bring him down.

00:32:39.890 --> 00:32:41.300
What is it?

00:32:41.300 --> 00:32:42.850
That instinct.

00:32:48.090 --> 00:32:50.240
Angels are our natural enemies.

00:32:51.390 --> 00:32:53.220
Even though it's unfitting,

00:32:54.620 --> 00:32:56.620
we immortal women are attracted to angels.

00:32:57.570 --> 00:32:58.700
Attracted, you say.

00:32:59.010 --> 00:33:01.320
Not mentally.

00:33:02.120 --> 00:33:03.160
Physically.

00:33:04.170 --> 00:33:05.960
We're sexually attracted to them.

00:33:06.280 --> 00:33:07.300
That's...

00:33:08.510 --> 00:33:10.550
In simple terms, we want them to embrace us.

00:33:11.240 --> 00:33:12.450
We can't help ourselves.

00:33:16.310 --> 00:33:19.030
Angels search for immortal women,

00:33:19.030 --> 00:33:21.510
embrace them, and then erase them.

00:33:22.780 --> 00:33:23.390
That's why...

00:33:24.740 --> 00:33:26.240
when we find angels,

00:33:26.240 --> 00:33:28.400
we must kill them.

00:33:30.220 --> 00:33:31.610
But Yuki-chan's brother is...

00:33:32.330 --> 00:33:33.490
No matter who it is.

00:33:52.750 --> 00:33:53.460
It's finally time.

00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:24.120
You are the Stamp?

00:34:27.930 --> 00:34:28.830
Ah, continue.

00:34:29.850 --> 00:34:32.580
I don't intend to interfere with your work.

00:34:33.780 --> 00:34:35.090
I can see very well from here.

00:34:35.860 --> 00:34:39.590
There are faint smells of gasoline throughout the park.

00:34:40.580 --> 00:34:44.310
The Secretary General is visiting a new city.

00:34:44.310 --> 00:34:47.010
In order to make it to the next dinner party on time,

00:34:47.010 --> 00:34:49.100
they are cutting through the park to get on the freeway.

00:34:51.770 --> 00:34:53.770
The sewage that flows beneath them underground

00:34:53.770 --> 00:34:56.860
has been mixed with gasoline and rigged with detonators.

00:34:57.380 --> 00:34:58.860
That will cause an explosion there.

00:35:03.040 --> 00:35:05.980
Then when the cars stop, you'll have your aiming point.

00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:14.180
The Secretary General's car is probably armored.

00:35:15.810 --> 00:35:17.500
That's why you need an RPG.

00:35:18.320 --> 00:35:21.040
And that's why you needed help from the Snakehead.

00:35:22.410 --> 00:35:25.550
Like I said, I won't interfere with your work.

00:35:26.060 --> 00:35:26.720
But...

00:35:27.780 --> 00:35:31.270
can you give back the Sutherland stamp you received as your payment?

00:35:41.150 --> 00:35:43.730
Secretary General Androvsky's car

00:35:43.730 --> 00:35:45.490
is now leaving the Metropolitan Government Office.

00:35:46.230 --> 00:35:48.490
The Secretary General is attending a dinner party

00:35:48.490 --> 00:35:50.460
at the State Guest House tonight.

00:35:51.170 --> 00:35:55.000
The Kuril Islands dispute, which has received a lot of attention lately, will be discussed tomorrow—

00:36:31.290 --> 00:36:32.180
Stop that.

00:36:33.460 --> 00:36:35.500
It's enough already.

00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:42.760
You already killed everyone who tried to bring you down, right?

00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:47.820
For your revenge...

00:36:48.700 --> 00:36:50.760
for Yuki-chan's sake...

00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:00.130
No...

00:37:00.890 --> 00:37:01.610
Don't come over here.

00:37:49.320 --> 00:37:50.030
Brother...

00:37:53.240 --> 00:37:54.030
I'll go.

00:37:54.860 --> 00:37:56.250
You wait here.

00:37:59.080 --> 00:37:59.860
Brother!

00:38:26.240 --> 00:38:26.780
The park?

00:38:29.400 --> 00:38:30.340
The angel is...

00:38:30.860 --> 00:38:32.610
Rin, please.

00:39:03.050 --> 00:39:03.900
Embrace me.

00:39:21.550 --> 00:39:22.570
Angels...

00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:26.870
consume us all...

00:40:01.180 --> 00:40:03.250
Yu... ki...

00:40:13.760 --> 00:40:14.810
I'm sorry.

00:40:15.250 --> 00:40:16.360
It's beautiful.

00:40:16.820 --> 00:40:18.890
A Fruit of Immortality that has absorbed blood.

00:40:19.390 --> 00:40:20.310
Apos.

00:40:21.180 --> 00:40:25.810
I didn't think you'd be eaten by an angel.

00:40:26.280 --> 00:40:28.190
Because you have that guy...

00:40:28.190 --> 00:40:28.900
Stop that.
Because you have that guy...

00:40:28.900 --> 00:40:29.420
Stop that.

00:40:29.420 --> 00:40:31.530
Don't you talk about him.

00:40:33.570 --> 00:40:34.700
Well, it's okay.

00:40:35.500 --> 00:40:37.280
Hey, can you give that to me?

00:40:38.060 --> 00:40:39.530
It was you, after all.

00:40:40.100 --> 00:40:40.880
Yeah.

00:40:41.420 --> 00:40:44.960
He was worried about his sister, even when he was about to die.

00:40:44.960 --> 00:40:47.250
I pitied him a bit.

00:40:47.250 --> 00:40:49.960
You told him about Yahagi and the others.

00:40:49.960 --> 00:40:52.050
I thought it would be a bit interesting.

00:40:52.650 --> 00:40:54.820
How much longer do you intend to toy with humans?

00:40:55.480 --> 00:40:59.050
Aren't you tired of living as a human being?

00:40:59.650 --> 00:41:01.160
They're fools.

00:41:01.640 --> 00:41:05.500
Doing meaningless things with their limited lives.

00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:07.560
They're helpless.

00:41:10.010 --> 00:41:12.010
I'm with them because they're helpless.

00:41:13.260 --> 00:41:17.030
Because they only have limited lives, they try to live to the fullest.

00:41:17.630 --> 00:41:19.700
Well, you could say that too.

00:41:23.390 --> 00:41:24.750
Go away already.

00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:28.130
Looks like I'm really hated.

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:30.250
I can't maintain this.

00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:36.140
Rin-san!

00:41:37.590 --> 00:41:38.450
Are you okay?

00:41:39.310 --> 00:41:40.300
Where is Shougo-san?

00:41:43.300 --> 00:41:44.850
You can see this too, right?

00:41:45.900 --> 00:41:48.020
A Fruit of Immortality that has absorbed human blood.

00:41:48.780 --> 00:41:49.540
This?

00:41:51.300 --> 00:41:52.280
Then...

00:41:54.630 --> 00:41:55.030
Rin-san?

00:41:55.640 --> 00:41:56.790
Leave me alone.

00:42:05.400 --> 00:42:07.070
Ken-chan, thank you for waiting.

00:42:09.120 --> 00:42:11.170
Not yet. I'm saving it.

00:42:28.930 --> 00:42:30.310
What happened here?

00:42:30.970 --> 00:42:32.480
What was that?

00:42:37.510 --> 00:42:39.460
For something like that...

00:42:40.250 --> 00:42:42.280
I made a mistake in my life.

00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:45.010
"Good things will happen as long as you're alive."

00:42:45.010 --> 00:42:46.290
I won't say something like that.

00:42:46.630 --> 00:42:51.420
But only you can give meaning to your life.

00:43:00.830 --> 00:43:02.750
It's okay. I know.

00:43:04.640 --> 00:43:05.930
My brother is dead, right?

00:43:10.500 --> 00:43:11.170
This is...

00:43:12.800 --> 00:43:15.440
The last thing your brother left behind.

00:45:01.740 --> 00:45:04.220
No, I wasn't crying.
